# Alva Docs Agent Brief

You are writing user-facing documentation for Alva, an AI business development platform. The site is published at `docs.alvahq.com`.

## Source of truth

The product repository is the source of truth. Read the relevant feature doc, then check the code for anything that matters (labels, defaults, limits, gates).

| Where | What |
|-------|------|
| `/Users/andrecox/Development/CRM/docs/features/*.md` | One internal doc per feature (read the folder; there are more than 30) |
| `/Users/andrecox/Development/CRM/docs/api/public-api-v1.md` | Public API |
| `/Users/andrecox/Development/CRM/CHANGELOG.md` and `docs/changelog-archive.md` | What shipped, and when |
| `/Users/andrecox/Development/CRM/app/(dashboard)/`, `components/`, `lib/` | Exact labels, defaults and limits |

Pull `dev` in that checkout before you start. Internal docs can lag the code, so do not copy a claim you have not checked. Anything under `docs/planning/` is not live: never document it.

## Audience

Founders, sales leaders and BDR managers. Non-technical. They do not know what a Server Action or a database column is.

## Never include

- The name of any third-party provider or AI model behind Alva (data, email, telephony, search, image or language model vendors, payments). The customer's own LinkedIn, Gmail, Google Workspace and Microsoft 365 accounts are fine.
- File paths, table or column names, enum values, environment variables, Alva tool names, System Admin internals.
- Prices or any amount System Admin can change (plan prices, starter credit, multipliers, add-on prices). Link to alvahq.com for pricing.
- Closed beta features that are not announced. Today that is LinkedIn messaging and the LinkedIn BDR agent. Signals is closed beta but documented, marked as closed beta and Pro.

## Tone and format

- UK English. Second person, active voice, sentence-case headings, **bold** for UI labels.
- Start with the first useful sentence. No "this guide will show you how to...". No history ("previously", "new in").
- Mintlify MDX with `title` and `description` frontmatter. Use the components already on the site: `<Note>`, `<Tip>`, `<Warning>`, `<Steps>`, `<CardGroup>`, `<AccordionGroup>`.
- Where Alva can do the task in chat, add a short "Ask Alva" section with example prompts.

## Navigation

New pages must be added to `docs.json`. Run `npx mint broken-links` before pushing.

## After writing

Commit and push to `main`. Mintlify deploys on every push.
